WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
Sri Lanka, in the 1st century BCE.

2
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:07.680
Monks are writing a vast collection
of teachings onto palm leaves.

3
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:11.150
They call it the Tipitaka: three baskets.

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.990
But the Buddha had lived
about four centuries earlier,

5
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.760
and he wrote nothing down.

6
00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.410
So how do Buddhists know what he taught?

7
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.760
In this mission, you'll open
each of the three baskets,

8
00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.730
from monastic rules to a
detailed analysis of the mind.

9
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.520
Then you'll see how the texts are
used in homes and temples today,

10
00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.770
from blessings to funerals.

11
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.970
Your mission: find out how Buddhists
know what the Buddha taught.
